    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a different telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). These generate the corresponding `OwnerDto` properties, which MapStruct auto-maps by name (same pattern as `namesakeCount`/`householdId`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persisted fields `possibleDuplicate` (`possible_duplicate` column) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`possible_duplicate_of` column) with getters/setters.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 Added `markPossibleDuplicate(Owner)`, called in `saveOwner` only when creating and **after** `assertIdentityUnique` (so hard duplicates are already rejected via `DuplicateIdentityException` before this runs). It scans existing owners for one matching normalized `lastName` (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) + exact `postcode` with a different normalized telephone, picking the lowest id on ties, and stamps `possibleDuplicate=true` / `possibleDuplicateOf=<id>`. Non-matches stay `false`/`null`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added `possible_duplicate BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` and `possible_duplicate_of INTEGER` to the `owners` table. `DEFAULT FALSE` keeps the seed rows (which use explicit column lists) non-null for the primitive `boolean` field.\n\nThe flag is determined once at creation time (like `namesakeCount`), so the first-created owner stays `possibleDuplicate=false` while the later soft-matching owner points back to it \u2014 matching the acceptance test's expectation.",
