        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the codebase's established structure cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit.** The soft-match logic lives as a private `markPossibleDuplicate(Owner)` helper in `ClinicServiceImpl`, invoked from `saveOwner` in the same `creating`-guarded style as the other creation-only steps (`countNamesakes`, `assertDailyCapacity`, `assertCityCapacity`). Placement directly after `assertIdentityUnique` matches its javadoc reference to that method.\n- **Consistent idiom, no new bad pattern.** The in-memory `ownerRepository.findAll()` scan with the `!existing.getId().equals(owner.getId())` self-exclusion and `normalizeHouseholdValue(...)` comparison mirrors `countNamesakes`, `findHouseholdMembers`, and `countOwnersInCity` almost exactly. It reuses the existing normalization helper rather than reinventing one, so it reads like the surrounding code.\n- **No catch-all growth / no duplication.** `Owner` just gains two persistent fields with plain getters/setters alongside the existing ones \u2014 no logic accretes in the entity. The schema change is applied uniformly across all four dialect files, and the OpenAPI additions are `readOnly` output fields consistent with the neighboring computed properties.\n\nNothing here warrants a structural change."
